    {
      "heading": {
        "text": "UNIT 300 — GAS DRYING AND MAIN AIR BLOWER",
        "level": 1
      },
      "level": 1,
      "paragraphs": [],
      "tables": []
    },
    {
      "heading": {
        "text": "Process Narrative",
        "level": 2
      },
      "level": 2,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Atmospheric air enters the drying tower (DT) through a coarse-mesh inlet filter and rises through structured packing irrigated with 93–96 wt% H₂SO₄ countercurrently. The desiccant acid absorbs moisture, reducing the air moisture content from ambient (up to 25 g/Nm³) to <0.1 g/Nm³ dry. The dried air exits through a fibre-bed mist eliminator to capture entrained acid droplets before passing to the centrifugal main air blower.",
          "style": "Normal"
        },
        {
          "text": "The main air blower is a single-stage centrifugal type (duty only; a full standby blower is provided) driven by a high-efficiency MV motor (11 kV) with Variable Frequency Drive (VFD). The VFD enables the blower to match air flow to the production rate setpoint from the DCS Master Load Governor. The blower operates at approximately 0.45 barg discharge pressure under normal conditions.",
          "style": "Normal"
        }
      ],
      "tables": []
    },
