    {
      "heading": {
        "text": "UNIT 700 — PRODUCT STORAGE AND LOADING",
        "level": 1
      },
      "level": 1,
      "paragraphs": [],
      "tables": []
    },
    {
      "heading": {
        "text": "Process Narrative",
        "level": 2
      },
      "level": 2,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Concentrated product acid is transferred from the FAT acid circuit to product storage tanks via the product acid cooler, where it is cooled to 25–40°C before entering storage. Product tanks are carbon steel construction with an internal rubber lining (natural rubber, 5 mm) or brick-lined; they are enclosed within a reinforced concrete bund of 110% tank capacity. Each tank is equipped with a fixed roof, nitrogen blanket (to prevent moisture ingress and vapour release), and level measurement with high-high level ESD shutdown. Product is dispatched via acid-proof centrifugal pumps to road tanker loading bays equipped with dry-break couplings and weigh-bridge control.",
          "style": "Normal"
        }
      ],
      "tables": []
    },
