    },
    {
      "text": "The process gas exits the furnace at 1,000–1,100°C into the Waste Heat Boiler (WHB), a fire-tube boiler design with process gas on the tube side. The WHB cools the gas from ~1,050°C to ~420°C while generating HP steam at 40 barg/400°C. A steam drum integral to the WHB package maintains water level; a three-element level control (LIC-201) regulates BFW admission.",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unit 200 — Operating Envelope Consistency Check",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "UNIT 300 — GAS DRYING AND MAIN AIR BLOWER",
      "style": "Heading 1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process Narrative",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atmospheric air enters the drying tower (DT) through a coarse-mesh inlet filter and rises through structured packing irrigated with 93–96 wt% H₂SO₄ countercurrently. The desiccant acid absorbs moisture, reducing the air moisture content from ambient (up to 25 g/Nm³) to <0.1 g/Nm³ dry. The dried air exits through a fibre-bed mist eliminator to capture entrained acid droplets before passing to the centrifugal main air blower.",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "The main air blower is a single-stage centrifugal type (duty only; a full standby blower is provided) driven by a high-efficiency MV motor (11 kV) with Variable Frequency Drive (VFD). The VFD enables the blower to match air flow to the production rate setpoint from the DCS Master Load Governor. The blower operates at approximately 0.45 barg discharge pressure under normal conditions.",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unit 300 — Operating Envelope Consistency Check",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "UNIT 400 — DCDA CATALYTIC CONVERTER",
      "style": "Heading 1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process Narrative",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "The converter is a vertical cylindrical carbon steel vessel with four catalyst beds (passes) arranged vertically. The shell operates at near-atmospheric pressure (slight positive, <0.15 barg). Between each pass, gas-to-gas heat exchangers (shell-and-tube, Type 304 SS) cool the reacted gas and preheat the incoming gas, maintaining each catalyst bed inlet within the optimal temperature window. Each bed contains Cs-promoted V₂O₅ catalyst (VK Series, Haldor Topsoe or equivalent). Catalyst bed depths are 1.2 m (Pass 1), 0.8 m (Pass 2), 0.8 m (Pass 3), 1.0 m (Pass 4).",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unit 400 — Operating Envelope Consistency Check",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "UNIT 500 — ABSORPTION SYSTEM (IPAT AND FAT)",
      "style": "Heading 1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process Narrative",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Both the Interpass Absorption Tower (IPAT) and Final Absorption Tower (FAT) are packed column vessels constructed of carbon steel with an internal monolithic brick lining (acid-resistant, silicate-bonded). Packing is ceramic Raschig rings (50 mm) or equivalent structured packing. Gas flows upward; acid flows downward (countercurrent). Product acid is continuously withdrawn from the absorption circuit, diluted with precise amounts of demineralised water, and cooled in shell-and-tube acid coolers (Saramet or Hastelloy C-276 tubed) before returning to the towers. The acid concentration is maintained at 98.0–98.5 wt% by the inline density-based control loop (AIC-501/502).",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unit 500 — Operating Envelope Consistency Check",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "UNIT 700 — PRODUCT STORAGE AND LOADING",
      "style": "Heading 1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process Narrative",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Concentrated product acid is transferred from the FAT acid circuit to product storage tanks via the product acid cooler, where it is cooled to 25–40°C before entering storage. Product tanks are carbon steel construction with an internal rubber lining (natural rubber, 5 mm) or brick-lined; they are enclosed within a reinforced concrete bund of 110% tank capacity. Each tank is equipped with a fixed roof, nitrogen blanket (to prevent moisture ingress and vapour release), and level measurement with high-high level ESD shutdown. Product is dispatched via acid-proof centrifugal pumps to road tanker loading bays equipped with dry-break couplings and weigh-bridge control.",
      "style": "Normal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unit 700 — Operating Envelope Consistency Check",
      "style": "Heading 2"
    }
  ],
